title: "Bear with ?!$%"*"
new-page: true

Is what Axel said to others. 

You always wondered why he was quick to your defence. Did you ever deserve that? No, what have you done for him? 

Pay for rent with whatever money you earned...Doing things? Half the time you leeched off him anyway.

He was ALWAYS rushing to your defence, he was telling others to show you grace.

There was one incident...You, bah. It was. How do you word it?

You were a shopkeeper, once. A...normal job. You were holding it together. You were exhausted, your mind felt like it was melting.

You felt that disgusting feeling again, the slythering snake in your gut, you felt the touches of everyone who wasn't there.

It reminded you of your youth.

You felt the disgusting things that were there. The way your throat bobbed up and down. The way your great big hands gripped the bread.

The way you towered over everyone else...Well, the women, you weren't that tall, but you were tall enough.

